  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ガラナ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AC%E3%83%A9%E3%83%8A",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 111116660,
      "text": "ガラナ(ポルトガル語: guaraná - グァラナ、学名：Paullinia cupana) は、ムクロジ科ガラナ属のつる植物。原産地はアマゾン川流域。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Guarana」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guarana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1373621068,
      "text": "Guaraná is a climbing plant in the family Sapindaceae, native to the Amazon basin and especially common in Brazil. Guaraná has large leaves and clusters of flowers, and is best known for the seeds from its beans, which are about the size of a coffee bean."
    }
  },
